WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.006 --> 00:00:09.009
[♪ epic theme music playing]

2
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:17.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

3
00:01:59.995 --> 00:02:01.371
[Orwyle]
I must see the queen.

4
00:02:02.456 --> 00:02:03.749
[door opens]

5
00:02:07.169 --> 00:02:08.253
Your Grace.

6
00:02:16.928 --> 00:02:17.971
[door opens]

7
00:02:21.433 --> 00:02:23.851
[Rhaenyra gasping]
He is risen.

8
00:02:23.852 --> 00:02:26.312
- Who?
- Aegon!

9
00:02:26.313 --> 00:02:27.773
Sunfyre is alive.

10
00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:29.941
Out!

11
00:02:32.778 --> 00:02:35.321
Sunfyre is dead.
rotting in a wasteland.

12
00:02:35.322 --> 00:02:37.032
[hyperventilating]

13
00:02:37.949 --> 00:02:39.201
- Oh.
- Sit down.

14
00:02:39.868 --> 00:02:42.662
Aegon burned
the Mooton host

15
00:02:42.663 --> 00:02:45.374
at Rook's Rest.
and then flew...

16
00:02:46.708 --> 00:02:48.335
I don't know where.

17
00:02:50.629 --> 00:02:53.298
His supporters have already sent
ravens throughout the realm...

18
00:02:54.466 --> 00:02:57.301
announcing the king's return.

19
00:02:57.302 --> 00:02:59.011
The smallfolk name it
a sign from the gods

20
00:02:59.012 --> 00:03:01.138
that Aegon is ordained to rule.
that he and his dragon

21
00:03:01.139 --> 00:03:03.809
have been resurrected
to reclaim the throne.

22
00:03:04.351 --> 00:03:06.977
At this moment.
mine own subjects

23
00:03:06.978 --> 00:03:09.146
gather outside the Grand Sept.
beseeching the gods

24
00:03:09.147 --> 00:03:10.731
to say who is meant
to rule them.

25
00:03:10.732 --> 00:03:13.401
After all for which
I have fought and suffered!

26
00:03:13.402 --> 00:03:14.403
Rhaenyra.

27
00:03:17.322 --> 00:03:19.324
[sobbing]

28
00:03:22.035 --> 00:03:24.037
[Daemon shushing]

29
00:03:26.415 --> 00:03:29.041
The lesser gods have no say
in what is to come.

30
00:03:29.042 --> 00:03:30.877
We are the blood
of Old Valyria.

31
00:03:33.088 --> 00:03:35.549
You have an absolute power
within your grasp.

32
00:03:36.675 --> 00:03:38.176
You have only to wield it.

33
00:03:40.429 --> 00:03:42.180
Fucking Viserys!

34
00:03:44.516 --> 00:03:47.017
He put me here.

35
00:03:47.018 --> 00:03:49.103
His prophecy has tested me
again and again.

36
00:03:49.104 --> 00:03:51.439
and I have met
its every challenge!

37
00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:53.442
[speaking High Valyrian]

38
00:04:20.552 --> 00:04:22.554
♪

39
00:05:54.312 --> 00:05:55.813
Your Grace.
have plans been laid

40
00:05:55.814 --> 00:05:57.148
for the Sea Snake's rescue?

41
00:05:59.317 --> 00:06:00.861
There will be a rescue?

42
00:06:03.321 --> 00:06:04.989
Your father
will search Tumbleton

43
00:06:04.990 --> 00:06:06.657
for the Sea Snake
once the town
has been reclaimed.

44
00:06:06.658 --> 00:06:08.993
He'll be long dead by then.

45
00:06:08.994 --> 00:06:11.161
- Send me now.
- [scoffs]

46
00:06:11.162 --> 00:06:13.497
You and Addam are needed here
to guard the city.

47
00:06:13.498 --> 00:06:16.041
if indeed these rumors are true

48
00:06:16.042 --> 00:06:17.836
and Sunfyre
was allowed to live.

49
00:06:18.879 --> 00:06:21.672
Corlys is your Hand.
your oldest ally.

50
00:06:21.673 --> 00:06:23.257
I do not wish
your grandsire ill.

51
00:06:23.258 --> 00:06:25.009
but he made his choice.

52
00:06:25.010 --> 00:06:26.761
and we must now
pay its price.

53
00:06:29.389 --> 00:06:30.515
It was your fault.

54
00:06:32.642 --> 00:06:33.893
What?

55
00:06:33.894 --> 00:06:36.103
That Lord Corlys
was out there to be taken.

56
00:06:36.104 --> 00:06:37.856
You do not dare.

57
00:06:38.732 --> 00:06:40.942
It is how you've always
treated those who serve you.

58
00:06:42.402 --> 00:06:44.945
Addam and I have labored
without rest

59
00:06:44.946 --> 00:06:47.448
over countless sorties
in search of your enemies.

60
00:06:47.449 --> 00:06:49.366
only to be repaid
in your anger.

61
00:06:49.367 --> 00:06:51.285
Yes. that is because
your sorties

62
00:06:51.286 --> 00:06:54.538
have yielded nothing.
while my enemies

63
00:06:54.539 --> 00:06:56.373
have been allowed
to muster their strength.

64
00:06:56.374 --> 00:06:59.044
If a person is useful to you.
you wield them.

65
00:07:00.253 --> 00:07:01.713
But if not.
you abandon them

66
00:07:02.631 --> 00:07:04.048
as you have with Rhaena.

67
00:07:04.049 --> 00:07:07.051
And now. she is broken.
like my grandsire.

68
00:07:07.052 --> 00:07:09.888
I would have been justified in
abandoning you after the Gullet.

69
00:07:11.222 --> 00:07:12.223
Perhaps.

70
00:07:13.224 --> 00:07:14.476
But you need my dragon.

71
00:07:18.229 --> 00:07:19.648
Insolent child.

72
00:07:21.441 --> 00:07:23.275
I should not blame you
for it truly.

73
00:07:23.276 --> 00:07:24.736
Insolence runs in your blood.

74
00:07:25.987 --> 00:07:28.073
As your sister
has lately reminded us.

75
00:07:34.621 --> 00:07:35.789
[sighs]

76
00:07:40.585 --> 00:07:42.628
[Alyn]
Good morrow. my lords.

77
00:07:42.629 --> 00:07:43.922
[Maynard]
"Good morrow." indeed.

78
00:07:45.423 --> 00:07:47.341
We've just sailed through
the night from Driftmark.

79
00:07:47.342 --> 00:07:50.595
after learning our Lord Admiral
is hostage to the Hightowers.

80
00:07:51.638 --> 00:07:55.100
The queen has called upon you
to secure King's Landing.

81
00:07:57.102 --> 00:07:59.478
To answer her could mean
our lord's death.

82
00:07:59.479 --> 00:08:02.273
Lord Corlys knew of the risks
of his adventures.

83
00:08:03.775 --> 00:08:06.360
He would want us to appraise
Velaryon honor

84
00:08:06.361 --> 00:08:07.779
as greater than his life.

85
00:08:09.030 --> 00:08:11.616
Who are you to speak
to our lord's desires?

86
00:08:13.118 --> 00:08:14.786
His eldest living son.

87
00:08:17.455 --> 00:08:18.873
And named successor.

88
00:08:20.834 --> 00:08:24.337
Your once and future
Lord of the Tides.

89
00:08:29.634 --> 00:08:31.344
[guard] Open the gates!

90
00:08:36.808 --> 00:08:39.059
[horses whinnying]

91
00:08:39.060 --> 00:08:42.063
[♪ dramatic music playing]

92
00:08:46.401 --> 00:08:47.527
About face!

93
00:08:48.737 --> 00:08:50.155
Forward march!

94
00:09:00.248 --> 00:09:01.249
That...

95
00:09:02.500 --> 00:09:05.211
all of it. is for you.

96
00:09:08.089 --> 00:09:09.507
Remarkable. is it not?

97
00:09:13.344 --> 00:09:14.345
But...

98
00:09:15.597 --> 00:09:17.390
you must be made a knight...

99
00:09:18.683 --> 00:09:20.351
before you can be crowned king.

100
00:09:21.728 --> 00:09:22.729
Kneel.

101
00:09:34.908 --> 00:09:36.784
Daeron Targaryen.

102
00:09:36.785 --> 00:09:40.079
do you swear before the eyes
of gods and men

103
00:09:40.080 --> 00:09:43.373
to defend those
who cannot defend themselves...

104
00:09:43.374 --> 00:09:46.418
- [people clamoring]
- [guard] Everyone inside!

105
00:09:46.419 --> 00:09:49.421
[Ormund]
<i>...to protect all women
and children...</i>

106
00:09:49.422 --> 00:09:51.466
[guard]
Come back here! Back!

107
00:09:52.383 --> 00:09:55.469
[Ormund]
<i>...to obey your captains.
your liege lord...</i>

108
00:09:55.470 --> 00:09:57.096
[guard] Seal the gates!

109
00:09:57.097 --> 00:09:59.224
[Ormund]
<i>...to fight bravely
whenever needed...</i>

110
00:10:00.809 --> 00:10:02.810
<i>and to do such other tasks</i>

111
00:10:02.811 --> 00:10:04.561
<i>- as are laid upon you...</i>
- Steady!

112
00:10:04.562 --> 00:10:06.063
<i>- ...however hard...</i>
- Hoist!

113
00:10:06.064 --> 00:10:08.774
<i>...or humble
or dangerous they may be?</i>

114
00:10:08.775 --> 00:10:09.776
Halt!

115
00:10:14.155 --> 00:10:15.323
I swear it.

116
00:10:22.831 --> 00:10:24.582
Then. rise a knight.

117
00:10:30.421 --> 00:10:32.257
Ser Daeron the Daring.

118
00:10:35.176 --> 00:10:37.095
And light the way.

119
00:10:43.351 --> 00:10:45.353
[Silverwing snarling]

120
00:10:48.982 --> 00:10:52.318
The Queen of Bastards' armies
are at the gates.

121
00:10:53.653 --> 00:10:55.988
And leading them
to the slaughter

122
00:10:55.989 --> 00:10:58.448
will be her uncle.
No. [snaps]

123
00:10:58.449 --> 00:11:00.367
- Her lover.
- [laughing]

124
00:11:00.368 --> 00:11:02.620
No. [snaps]
Her husband.

125
00:11:04.455 --> 00:11:07.250
Daemon fucking Targaryen.

126
00:11:08.334 --> 00:11:11.129
- And his dragon.
- Of course he's got
a fucking dragon!

127
00:11:13.798 --> 00:11:15.216
But he's not gonna use it.

128
00:11:17.468 --> 00:11:19.052
And how do you know?

129
00:11:19.053 --> 00:11:23.141
'Cause his lady wife.
the queen. won't let him.

130
00:11:24.809 --> 00:11:27.520
Rhaenyra's got Daemon
on a short lead.

131
00:11:28.646 --> 00:11:31.149
Like a bitch in a kennel.

132
00:11:34.152 --> 00:11:36.154
Another ale for the dragonlord.

133
00:11:38.239 --> 00:11:42.159
The Rogue Prince
will soon quake

134
00:11:42.160 --> 00:11:46.580
before the mighty and terrible

135
00:11:46.581 --> 00:11:48.666
Lord Ulf the White!

136
00:11:56.257 --> 00:11:57.675
[Elinda] Your Grace.

137
00:11:59.510 --> 00:12:01.261
Y-Your Grace.
is aught amiss?

138
00:12:01.262 --> 00:12:02.513
What is it?

139
00:12:03.848 --> 00:12:05.725
The Princess Helaena.

140
00:12:06.684 --> 00:12:08.436
She still has not taken food.

141
00:12:09.687 --> 00:12:12.231
The maesters
worry for her health.

142
00:12:12.232 --> 00:12:14.525
especially for the babe
in her belly.

143
00:12:20.448 --> 00:12:21.866
Summon Ser Alyn.

144
00:12:24.911 --> 00:12:27.038
I require a full escort
to the Grand Sept.

145
00:12:27.705 --> 00:12:31.375
There. today.
the High Septon
will anoint me

146
00:12:31.376 --> 00:12:33.962
and bless my reign for all
of King's Landing to see.

147
00:12:35.046 --> 00:12:37.548
There will be no doubt who
the gods have chosen to rule.

148
00:12:39.050 --> 00:12:40.551
At once. Your Grace.

149
00:12:42.095 --> 00:12:43.388
Will that be all?

150
00:12:50.061 --> 00:12:51.062
No.

151
00:12:54.732 --> 00:12:55.733
[door opens]

152
00:12:58.736 --> 00:12:59.821
What is this?

153
00:13:00.613 --> 00:13:01.822
Sers.

154
00:13:01.823 --> 00:13:04.032
- Sers!
- [Elinda] My lady.

155
00:13:04.033 --> 00:13:06.660
Beg pardon for the intrusion.
We weren't given much time.

156
00:13:06.661 --> 00:13:08.245
Time for what?

157
00:13:08.246 --> 00:13:10.914
Your passage
has been arranged aboard
the <i>Mermaid's Kiss.</i>

158
00:13:10.915 --> 00:13:13.750
You are to sail
for Pentos at dusk.

159
00:13:13.751 --> 00:13:16.461
I am to inform you

160
00:13:16.462 --> 00:13:18.422
that your services here
are at an end.

161
00:13:18.423 --> 00:13:19.965
[items clattering]

162
00:13:19.966 --> 00:13:22.843
You have served the queen
and the realm most faithfully.

163
00:13:22.844 --> 00:13:25.429
and Her Grace wishes
to extend her gratitude.

164
00:13:25.430 --> 00:13:27.180
[clattering continues]

165
00:13:27.181 --> 00:13:29.683
You will be provided with gold
sufficient for a manse

166
00:13:29.684 --> 00:13:31.269
and servants of your own.

167
00:13:32.478 --> 00:13:34.438
[clattering continues]

168
00:13:34.439 --> 00:13:35.773
Be quick about it.

169
00:13:39.277 --> 00:13:41.821
I-- I do not understand either.
my lady.

170
00:13:48.619 --> 00:13:50.621
[wind swishing]

171
00:13:53.374 --> 00:13:55.335
The hour has passed.
my lady.

172
00:13:57.462 --> 00:13:59.297
I must return you
to your quarters.

173
00:14:09.849 --> 00:14:11.851
[horse nickering]

174
00:14:22.487 --> 00:14:24.155
This way. princess.

175
00:14:34.165 --> 00:14:35.166
[door opens]

176
00:14:40.588 --> 00:14:42.506
Do not trust the queen.

177
00:14:42.507 --> 00:14:44.841
Aegon has returned.
His dragon lives.

178
00:14:44.842 --> 00:14:47.177
Your unborn child
is a hostage.

179
00:14:47.178 --> 00:14:49.679
a prize by which
she can hold power

180
00:14:49.680 --> 00:14:51.223
- over her enemies.
- [guard] Keep moving.

181
00:14:51.224 --> 00:14:53.434
- Enough.
- She will never release you.

182
00:15:04.445 --> 00:15:06.196
[Aemond's voice echoing]
<i>Do you remember?</i>

183
00:15:06.197 --> 00:15:09.242
- [echoed screaming]
<i>- Do you remember?</i>

184
00:15:12.078 --> 00:15:13.371
<i>Help me.</i>

185
00:15:16.541 --> 00:15:18.250
[Alys] Fret not.

186
00:15:18.251 --> 00:15:19.544
You're alive.

187
00:15:22.046 --> 00:15:23.130
Here.

188
00:15:23.131 --> 00:15:24.382
Drink this.

189
00:15:26.134 --> 00:15:27.552
There'll be another in an hour.

190
00:15:28.970 --> 00:15:31.054
She poisoned me.

191
00:15:31.055 --> 00:15:34.474
You have realized
you're alone in this world.

192
00:15:34.475 --> 00:15:36.060
In that. we are together.

193
00:15:43.734 --> 00:15:44.985
[Aemond groaning softly]

194
00:15:44.986 --> 00:15:47.071
But I no longer wish
to suffer it.

195
00:15:49.574 --> 00:15:51.074
Do you?

196
00:15:51.075 --> 00:15:52.910
Why do you care
whether I am alone?

197
00:15:54.412 --> 00:15:56.414
Whether I live or die?

198
00:15:59.584 --> 00:16:02.003
I'm a kinslayer. Alys.

199
00:16:03.921 --> 00:16:07.550
My own brother
is dead by my hand.

200
00:16:08.301 --> 00:16:11.596
I have been damned
for my trespasses
and cursed to suffer.

201
00:16:14.182 --> 00:16:16.350
- You should abandon me.
- [scoffs softly]

202
00:16:17.894 --> 00:16:20.188
Lest you bring mine own fate
upon yourself.

203
00:16:26.736 --> 00:16:29.529
When the dragon Balerion
burned this place.

204
00:16:29.530 --> 00:16:31.824
it was to end
Lord Harren's line.

205
00:16:33.326 --> 00:16:35.786
But his line
was not so easily ended.

206
00:16:37.288 --> 00:16:38.456
A child. a...

207
00:16:39.832 --> 00:16:40.833
a boy...

208
00:16:42.627 --> 00:16:43.794
lived on.

209
00:16:44.795 --> 00:16:47.715
Burned terribly.
but alive.

210
00:16:49.800 --> 00:16:52.303
His mother would have
given anything to save him.

211
00:16:56.140 --> 00:17:00.060
She summoned maesters
from across the Seven Kingdoms.

212
00:17:00.061 --> 00:17:01.395
but to no avail.

213
00:17:08.486 --> 00:17:10.821
So. she turned to older cures.

214
00:17:12.073 --> 00:17:15.742
She uncovered incantations
more ancient than the land.

215
00:17:15.743 --> 00:17:19.330
She treated with things
that lived in the forest.

216
00:17:22.542 --> 00:17:25.836
But none of it could unmake
what dragonfire made.

217
00:17:27.755 --> 00:17:29.215
And when the boy was gone...

218
00:17:36.347 --> 00:17:38.683
she tr-- she tried
to go with him.

219
00:17:49.527 --> 00:17:52.029
And that is when
she learned the cost.

220
00:17:54.448 --> 00:17:55.908
[sniffling]

221
00:17:58.286 --> 00:18:00.538
She discovered then
she was cursed.

222
00:18:01.205 --> 00:18:02.456
To live on...

223
00:18:04.250 --> 00:18:08.462
to remain within the bounds
of the river kings of old...

224
00:18:09.380 --> 00:18:11.923
cursed for sharing
in Harren's avarice.

225
00:18:11.924 --> 00:18:14.884
Stripped of her name.
her title.

226
00:18:14.885 --> 00:18:16.304
her castle.
[sniffling]

227
00:18:18.222 --> 00:18:21.099
And sentenced to serve
every ha'penny lord

228
00:18:21.100 --> 00:18:22.892
who came here to rule it.

229
00:18:22.893 --> 00:18:25.437
That was a hundred years past.

230
00:18:25.438 --> 00:18:27.481
It's a long time
to be alone.

231
00:18:30.276 --> 00:18:33.279
[♪ soft. dramatic music playing]

232
00:18:56.260 --> 00:18:57.970
You must eat. sister.

233
00:18:59.096 --> 00:19:00.681
[door closes]

234
00:19:04.602 --> 00:19:05.978
Think of the babe.

235
00:19:06.937 --> 00:19:08.648
You are thinking
of him now. too?

236
00:19:10.358 --> 00:19:13.611
You're saying it's a boy?
Do you know this?

237
00:19:16.030 --> 00:19:17.198
Look at me.

238
00:19:26.999 --> 00:19:28.793
You cannot think
I would harm you.

239
00:19:29.585 --> 00:19:32.505
Do you think life is nothing
more than not being dead?

240
00:19:34.131 --> 00:19:35.466
[sighs]

241
00:19:36.717 --> 00:19:39.136
Our father
would hate you for this.

242
00:19:42.223 --> 00:19:44.392
And yet he did nothing
to prevent it.

243
00:19:45.685 --> 00:19:49.145
I strove to honor
his philosophy

244
00:19:49.146 --> 00:19:51.815
until I saw that it would be
the realm's undoing.

245
00:19:51.816 --> 00:19:56.319
There is a beetle that emerges
on the cusp of summer.

246
00:19:56.320 --> 00:19:58.029
It has lots of colors.

247
00:19:58.030 --> 00:20:01.325
Blue. gold. purples.

248
00:20:02.660 --> 00:20:04.203
It looks like a turtle.

249
00:20:05.996 --> 00:20:07.707
Have you ever noticed it?

250
00:20:08.916 --> 00:20:10.542
I can't say I have.

251
00:20:10.543 --> 00:20:13.336
You can only find it
in King's Landing.

252
00:20:13.337 --> 00:20:16.716
It sustains itself on the waste
of other creatures.

253
00:20:21.387 --> 00:20:22.513
It's beautiful.

254
00:20:23.681 --> 00:20:25.515
[chuckles softly]

255
00:20:25.516 --> 00:20:27.852
Well. when summer returns.
you will have to show me.

256
00:20:34.942 --> 00:20:36.861
You don't care about it.

257
00:20:39.530 --> 00:20:40.698
You're pretending.

258
00:20:42.783 --> 00:20:47.037
All the things you care about
are ugly.

259
00:20:48.873 --> 00:20:50.458
This place...

260
00:20:51.709 --> 00:20:52.918
is ugly.

261
00:20:54.920 --> 00:20:56.713
[sighs]

262
00:20:56.714 --> 00:20:58.883
You. yourself...

263
00:21:00.384 --> 00:21:01.551
ugly.

264
00:21:01.552 --> 00:21:02.553
Eat.

265
00:21:03.846 --> 00:21:05.556
Or you will force my hand.

266
00:21:33.918 --> 00:21:34.919
No.

267
00:21:35.836 --> 00:21:37.087
No! No!

268
00:21:37.838 --> 00:21:40.089
No! No! No!

269
00:21:40.090 --> 00:21:41.925
Stop! Stop.

270
00:21:41.926 --> 00:21:43.928
[panicked breathing]

271
00:21:46.639 --> 00:21:48.641
[muffled screaming]

272
00:21:50.100 --> 00:21:52.102
[choking]

273
00:21:53.312 --> 00:21:55.314
[coughing]

274
00:21:57.358 --> 00:21:58.943
[guard] Forward march!

275
00:22:04.281 --> 00:22:06.283
[guard shouting indistinctly]

276
00:22:10.663 --> 00:22:11.664
[Addam] Brother.

277
00:22:13.332 --> 00:22:15.208
Will you march
on Tumbleton as well?

278
00:22:15.209 --> 00:22:17.628
No. Today we guard the queen
in her purpose.

279
00:22:18.963 --> 00:22:20.339
Where does she go?

280
00:22:24.802 --> 00:22:28.429
News of Aegon's return has set
the queen on a dark path.

281
00:22:28.430 --> 00:22:31.140
She has grounded Baela
and confined her to the Keep.

282
00:22:31.141 --> 00:22:32.809
Did you know this?

283
00:22:32.810 --> 00:22:34.811
These are dangerous days.

284
00:22:34.812 --> 00:22:37.648
and it is not mine
to question Her Grace.

285
00:22:40.484 --> 00:22:41.985
Why would you?

286
00:22:41.986 --> 00:22:45.321
While our father awaits
the Hightower gallows.

287
00:22:45.322 --> 00:22:48.157
Rhaenyra raises you up
in his place.

288
00:22:48.158 --> 00:22:50.493
A glorious ascent for a bastard.

289
00:22:50.494 --> 00:22:53.329
[guards shouting indistinctly]

290
00:22:53.330 --> 00:22:56.834
I have no ambition
but to discharge my duty.

291
00:22:58.043 --> 00:22:59.919
Be ready!

292
00:22:59.920 --> 00:23:02.923
[♪ dramatic music playing]

293
00:23:14.184 --> 00:23:15.351
[Alyn] Form up!

294
00:23:15.352 --> 00:23:16.520
[guard] Form up!

295
00:23:22.443 --> 00:23:23.444
March!

296
00:23:35.205 --> 00:23:37.207
[soldiers chattering]

297
00:23:44.089 --> 00:23:45.215
[Daeron] Gods.

298
00:23:46.800 --> 00:23:48.385
How will we face them all?

299
00:23:49.553 --> 00:23:52.431
Bravely and pointlessly.

300
00:23:53.557 --> 00:23:55.725
Take your places. boys.

301
00:23:55.726 --> 00:23:57.811
Keep coming. take your places.

302
00:23:59.480 --> 00:24:00.940
Keep coming. Be brave.

303
00:24:02.691 --> 00:24:04.944
Put the boys to the front.
They must be seen.

304
00:24:06.904 --> 00:24:09.989
My lord. Ulf hasn't reported.

305
00:24:09.990 --> 00:24:11.408
and he's not with his dragon.

306
00:24:16.830 --> 00:24:18.748
Take a tithing of men
off each post.

307
00:24:18.749 --> 00:24:19.749
Search the town.

308
00:24:19.750 --> 00:24:20.833
Find him.

309
00:24:20.834 --> 00:24:22.001
[Roxton]
You! With me.

310
00:24:22.002 --> 00:24:23.587
- Something's wrong.
- Yes.

311
00:24:24.505 --> 00:24:26.297
We're all going to die.

312
00:24:26.298 --> 00:24:27.466
No.

313
00:24:28.133 --> 00:24:29.593
With Uncle.

314
00:24:30.594 --> 00:24:33.138
He and Roxton
have some secret plot afoot.

315
00:24:35.474 --> 00:24:37.141
He has kept it even from me.

316
00:24:37.142 --> 00:24:39.352
- [Gwayne] Whatever it was...
- Get away from me!

317
00:24:39.353 --> 00:24:41.855
...it has not appeared
to have come to pass.

318
00:24:45.109 --> 00:24:46.484
Please!

319
00:24:46.485 --> 00:24:48.027
Please. ser.
we don't want to do it.

320
00:24:48.028 --> 00:24:49.612
- I just want to go home
to my mom.
- Don't make us.

321
00:24:49.613 --> 00:24:50.822
[children begging]

322
00:24:50.823 --> 00:24:52.533
I must take wing
against the enemy.

323
00:24:53.701 --> 00:24:54.702
No!

324
00:24:55.869 --> 00:24:59.790
All these men. these boys.
are here for me.

325
00:25:01.458 --> 00:25:04.252
- I cannot let them fight alone.
- For what purpose. boy?

326
00:25:04.253 --> 00:25:06.462
To become another body
amongst Ormund's countless dead?

327
00:25:06.463 --> 00:25:08.548
What are my choices?

328
00:25:08.549 --> 00:25:11.218
I either fight. or I flee.

329
00:25:12.136 --> 00:25:13.553
[sighs]

330
00:25:13.554 --> 00:25:15.556
[dragon bellowing]

331
00:25:17.349 --> 00:25:18.976
Mayhaps there is another.

332
00:25:21.812 --> 00:25:23.230
[soldier] Dragon!

333
00:25:24.231 --> 00:25:26.316
[all shouting]

334
00:25:29.319 --> 00:25:31.321
[Caraxes whistles]

335
00:25:32.865 --> 00:25:34.867
[chuckles]

336
00:25:36.660 --> 00:25:40.246
[♪ dramatic music playing]

337
00:25:40.247 --> 00:25:41.999
[Ormund]
Ulf the Dragonrider!

338
00:25:43.167 --> 00:25:45.251
I'm looking for
Ulf the Dragonrider.

339
00:25:45.252 --> 00:25:47.588
- Ulf!
- [Caraxes screeching]

340
00:25:48.547 --> 00:25:49.840
Ulf!

341
00:25:54.261 --> 00:25:58.097
And now. Lord Ormund's boy king
and his faithful squire.

342
00:25:58.098 --> 00:25:59.682
Shut up.

343
00:25:59.683 --> 00:26:02.727
Driftmark lies in ruin.
your legacy in tatters.

344
00:26:02.728 --> 00:26:06.439
But King Daeron. in all
his generosity and wisdom.

345
00:26:06.440 --> 00:26:07.774
can offer a richer future

346
00:26:07.775 --> 00:26:10.068
than the one Rhaenyra
has laid for you.

347
00:26:10.069 --> 00:26:12.112
My honor is all
that remains to me.

348
00:26:13.530 --> 00:26:16.783
Do you really think I would
hawk it for Hightower coin?

349
00:26:16.784 --> 00:26:18.576
[Gwayne] Very well.

350
00:26:18.577 --> 00:26:20.120
The hard road. then.

351
00:26:22.790 --> 00:26:24.874
[bell tolling]

352
00:26:24.875 --> 00:26:26.877
[townsfolk chattering]

353
00:26:37.471 --> 00:26:38.597
[guard] Make way!

354
00:26:39.723 --> 00:26:40.974
Clear the way!

355
00:26:42.267 --> 00:26:45.646
- Move back!
- Get back! Get back!

356
00:26:46.396 --> 00:26:48.649
- Move! Clear the way!
- [people shouting]

357
00:26:49.900 --> 00:26:51.902
- Get back!
- [horse whinnying]

358
00:26:53.946 --> 00:26:55.948
[guards continue shouting]

359
00:26:58.283 --> 00:27:00.244
[bell tolling]

360
00:27:07.251 --> 00:27:08.752
[guard] Get back!

361
00:27:14.925 --> 00:27:16.843
You are my heir now. Joffrey.

362
00:27:16.844 --> 00:27:19.220
and the duty I pass to you

363
00:27:19.221 --> 00:27:20.931
is more than simple rule.

364
00:27:24.101 --> 00:27:27.103
There is a story
that your grandsire told me.

365
00:27:27.104 --> 00:27:29.273
It was told to him
by the Old King.

366
00:27:30.357 --> 00:27:32.192
And I passed it on...

367
00:27:33.485 --> 00:27:34.778
to your brother...

368
00:27:36.655 --> 00:27:38.531
following mine own ascent.

369
00:27:38.532 --> 00:27:40.534
[bellowing]

370
00:27:44.288 --> 00:27:46.455
Tumbleton. my lords!

371
00:27:46.456 --> 00:27:47.708
At long last.

372
00:27:49.793 --> 00:27:51.294
[Oscar Tully]
If it weren't for Cole.

373
00:27:51.295 --> 00:27:52.712
we'd have been here
a fortnight ago.

374
00:27:52.713 --> 00:27:55.673
So easy to forget about him.
Do tell me how he died.

375
00:27:55.674 --> 00:27:56.841
Badly.

376
00:27:56.842 --> 00:27:58.635
[Caraxes whistling]

377
00:28:00.137 --> 00:28:03.306
My prince. my lords.
a Hightower knight approaches.

378
00:28:03.307 --> 00:28:05.558
So? Kill him.

379
00:28:05.559 --> 00:28:06.894
With Lord Corlys.

380
00:28:09.188 --> 00:28:10.313
Hyah.

381
00:28:10.314 --> 00:28:13.650
[♪ dramatic music playing]

382
00:28:22.993 --> 00:28:25.036
[Gwayne]
Prince Daemon.

383
00:28:25.037 --> 00:28:26.662
I am Ser Gwayne Hightower.

384
00:28:26.663 --> 00:28:28.372
Well met.

385
00:28:28.373 --> 00:28:29.875
[Roderick]
Fuck me.

386
00:28:30.834 --> 00:28:32.627
[chuckles]

387
00:28:32.628 --> 00:28:34.838
I've seen more meat
on a butcher's knife.

388
00:28:36.840 --> 00:28:38.174
Can I kill him?

389
00:28:38.175 --> 00:28:40.593
[Gwayne coughs]
You already know Lord Corlys.

390
00:28:40.594 --> 00:28:41.678
Are you well?

391
00:28:42.721 --> 00:28:43.764
I'm well enough.

392
00:28:46.600 --> 00:28:48.267
So. speak.

393
00:28:48.268 --> 00:28:51.354
My cousin Ormund
has taken leave of his senses.

394
00:28:51.355 --> 00:28:53.064
He would rather die
than admit defeat.

395
00:28:53.065 --> 00:28:54.191
And you?

396
00:28:55.067 --> 00:28:56.526
Well. I'm not blind.

397
00:28:57.736 --> 00:28:59.863
I know we will not survive
the day if you attack.

398
00:29:01.114 --> 00:29:02.699
So. as a token of good faith...

399
00:29:06.370 --> 00:29:08.371
- I return your Hand.
- [chains rattling]

400
00:29:08.372 --> 00:29:11.375
[scoffs]
Four fingers of him. at least.

401
00:29:12.125 --> 00:29:13.376
I have come to sue for peace.

402
00:29:13.377 --> 00:29:15.544
- [laughing]
- To plead with you

403
00:29:15.545 --> 00:29:17.380
at the behest
of Daeron Targaryen.

404
00:29:17.381 --> 00:29:21.300
[chuckles] The latest
in your line of false kings.

405
00:29:21.301 --> 00:29:22.885
[Daemon] The war will end
when all the traitors' heads

406
00:29:22.886 --> 00:29:24.972
are mounted on spikes
above the King's Gate...

407
00:29:25.973 --> 00:29:27.139
and not before.

408
00:29:27.140 --> 00:29:28.934
[Gwayne]
Listen to Daeron's entreaty.

409
00:29:29.726 --> 00:29:31.102
Divide the realm.

410
00:29:31.103 --> 00:29:33.229
Let the queen rule
over the Crownlands.
the North.

411
00:29:33.230 --> 00:29:35.064
the Vale. all the lands
watered by the Trident.

412
00:29:35.065 --> 00:29:38.109
and let Daeron
rule from Oldtown.

413
00:29:38.110 --> 00:29:39.820
Oh. please!

414
00:29:40.988 --> 00:29:44.240
Let me kill this milk-suck
southerling cunt.

415
00:29:44.241 --> 00:29:46.284
The realm was once
seven kingdoms.

416
00:29:46.285 --> 00:29:47.952
before the Conqueror.
when we were divided

417
00:29:47.953 --> 00:29:49.412
- but at peace--
- Stop!

418
00:29:49.413 --> 00:29:51.289
My good Lord Hand.

419
00:29:51.290 --> 00:29:53.040
I thought the Hightowers

420
00:29:53.041 --> 00:29:54.960
might have cut off
your tongue as well.

421
00:29:58.005 --> 00:29:59.339
Hightower is not wrong.

422
00:30:00.299 --> 00:30:02.300
There are great houses
who still hold to the precedent

423
00:30:02.301 --> 00:30:06.095
set by the Great Council
that a woman cannot rule.

424
00:30:06.096 --> 00:30:08.639
It was your wife
who was passed over. Corlys.

425
00:30:08.640 --> 00:30:10.766
Rhaenyra seized the throne
with a horde of dragons.

426
00:30:10.767 --> 00:30:12.268
Her rule is now unassailable.

427
00:30:12.269 --> 00:30:14.353
The queen
has many dragons. yes.

428
00:30:14.354 --> 00:30:15.939
but the great houses hesitate.

429
00:30:17.107 --> 00:30:19.818
Her subjects do not feel safe.
nor should they.

430
00:30:20.944 --> 00:30:22.821
Aemond and Vhagar
remain at large.

431
00:30:28.035 --> 00:30:29.785
[chain rattling]

432
00:30:29.786 --> 00:30:31.704
Give Prince Daeron Oldtown.

433
00:30:31.705 --> 00:30:34.957
Name him Lord Paramount
of the Reach.

434
00:30:34.958 --> 00:30:37.209
Daeron will never be king.

435
00:30:37.210 --> 00:30:39.670
but he and his dragon
can be wardens of the South.

436
00:30:39.671 --> 00:30:41.715
That wasn't what I was offering.

437
00:30:44.384 --> 00:30:46.177
Wed Daeron to Rhaena.

438
00:30:46.178 --> 00:30:48.137
Seal the breach
between your houses.

439
00:30:48.138 --> 00:30:50.389
With the combined will
of King's Landing.

440
00:30:50.390 --> 00:30:52.683
the Reach. the North.
the Riverlands.

441
00:30:52.684 --> 00:30:54.977
and the Vale. Rhaenyra
can quickly bring the West

442
00:30:54.978 --> 00:30:57.229
and the Stormlands to heel.

443
00:30:57.230 --> 00:30:58.981
And what will
the usurper Aegon say

444
00:30:58.982 --> 00:31:00.900
when he hears of this pact?

445
00:31:00.901 --> 00:31:04.487
He now scuttles about somewhere
on his crippled dragon.

446
00:31:04.488 --> 00:31:06.989
half-cooked.
but still fit to rule.

447
00:31:06.990 --> 00:31:08.575
Or so he thinks.

448
00:31:09.993 --> 00:31:11.244
Was that news?

449
00:31:12.829 --> 00:31:15.790
It is so tragic to see
brother set against brother.

450
00:31:15.791 --> 00:31:18.501
Aegon and Aemond
would be common enemies
of this new alliance.

451
00:31:18.502 --> 00:31:19.878
Alliance?

452
00:31:21.129 --> 00:31:25.049
I never took you for a traitor.
Corlys. and worse. a craven.

453
00:31:25.050 --> 00:31:27.761
What price has the boy king
offered for your fealty?

454
00:31:28.929 --> 00:31:29.930
Peace.

455
00:31:31.181 --> 00:31:34.183
Two paths
diverge before you. Daemon.

456
00:31:34.184 --> 00:31:36.185
but both lead to the same end.

457
00:31:36.186 --> 00:31:40.356
Rhaenyra sitting the Iron Throne
ruling the Seven Kingdoms.

458
00:31:40.357 --> 00:31:42.067
All that remains
for you to decide...

459
00:31:43.527 --> 00:31:46.237
is what you want
from this war.

460
00:31:46.238 --> 00:31:47.531
Victory?

461
00:31:49.032 --> 00:31:50.742
Or a mountain
of dead Hightowers?

462
00:31:52.202 --> 00:31:54.120
What do you think?

463
00:31:54.121 --> 00:31:56.455
You would callously cast away
the lives of thou--

464
00:31:56.456 --> 00:31:59.083
[choking]

465
00:31:59.084 --> 00:32:01.544
No one will rule but Rhaenyra.

466
00:32:01.545 --> 00:32:04.130
the ordained
Queen of the Andals.
of the First Men.

467
00:32:04.131 --> 00:32:06.382
of beggars and thieves
and cowards like you.

468
00:32:06.383 --> 00:32:08.717
A new Valyria
will rise from the ashes

469
00:32:08.718 --> 00:32:10.428
of her usurper half-brothers

470
00:32:10.429 --> 00:32:12.596
and of the Hightowers
of Oldtown.

471
00:32:12.597 --> 00:32:15.933
Now. you came to me
under a banner of peace.

472
00:32:15.934 --> 00:32:18.060
so I will give you the choice.

473
00:32:18.061 --> 00:32:21.272
Die here.
or behind those walls.

474
00:32:21.273 --> 00:32:23.608
like the rodent you are.

475
00:32:24.609 --> 00:32:26.068
[Gwayne coughing]

476
00:32:26.069 --> 00:32:27.611
Lord Corlys is my prisoner.

477
00:32:27.612 --> 00:32:29.488
Hightower may return
to alert his cousin

478
00:32:29.489 --> 00:32:32.658
- to our imminent coming.
- Get up! Get up! [shouting]

479
00:32:32.659 --> 00:32:34.118
[Daemon]
Bring the ladders and the rams

480
00:32:34.119 --> 00:32:35.578
and form up to march.

481
00:32:35.579 --> 00:32:37.788
The next man
to stall on this attack

482
00:32:37.789 --> 00:32:41.584
will be tied to the front
of my fucking horse!

483
00:32:41.585 --> 00:32:43.587
[breathing heavily]

484
00:32:44.629 --> 00:32:46.590
- [distant dragon screeching]
- [gasps]

485
00:32:47.924 --> 00:32:49.634
[dragon wings flapping]

486
00:32:52.137 --> 00:32:54.139
[faint screeching]

487
00:33:00.270 --> 00:33:03.607
- [dragon screeching]
- [wings flapping]

488
00:33:09.821 --> 00:33:11.823
[dragon screeching]

489
00:33:16.286 --> 00:33:19.997
- [wings flapping]
- [dragon snarling]

490
00:33:19.998 --> 00:33:22.000
[dragon screeching]

491
00:33:27.964 --> 00:33:29.966
[wheezing]

492
00:33:33.470 --> 00:33:35.472
[chittering]

493
00:33:37.307 --> 00:33:39.309
[breathing heavily]

494
00:33:46.358 --> 00:33:47.817
It cannot be.

495
00:33:48.860 --> 00:33:50.195
You are dead.

496
00:33:51.988 --> 00:33:52.989
[smacking]

497
00:33:56.326 --> 00:33:57.577
I'm alive!

498
00:33:59.496 --> 00:34:00.497
Imbecile.

499
00:34:03.500 --> 00:34:06.001
Brother. Brother.

500
00:34:06.002 --> 00:34:07.879
I beg for your forgiveness.

501
00:34:10.173 --> 00:34:12.592
[giggling]

502
00:34:14.427 --> 00:34:16.429
[laughing]

503
00:34:19.516 --> 00:34:20.725
Forgiveness?

504
00:34:24.854 --> 00:34:26.856
I should split you in half.

505
00:34:29.693 --> 00:34:30.694
Hm?

506
00:34:32.362 --> 00:34:34.698
I should have Sunfyre
burn you alive.

507
00:34:35.949 --> 00:34:39.286
Mm. but slowly.

508
00:34:40.704 --> 00:34:42.706
So I can see your skin...

509
00:34:43.748 --> 00:34:46.710
peel and blister.

510
00:34:47.419 --> 00:34:48.878
You kinslayer.

511
00:34:50.880 --> 00:34:52.632
[whispering]
You usurper.

512
00:34:54.759 --> 00:34:55.760
You cunt!

513
00:35:04.227 --> 00:35:05.228
No.

514
00:35:07.439 --> 00:35:10.399
No. no. no. no. no. no. no!

515
00:35:10.400 --> 00:35:12.067
I was supposed to enjoy this.

516
00:35:12.068 --> 00:35:13.445
What's wrong with you?

517
00:35:15.739 --> 00:35:16.906
Fight me!

518
00:35:18.283 --> 00:35:19.409
[sighs]

519
00:35:21.786 --> 00:35:24.246
I coveted what you had

520
00:35:24.247 --> 00:35:25.998
and judged you unsuited
for the crown.

521
00:35:25.999 --> 00:35:27.416
Oh.

522
00:35:27.417 --> 00:35:29.419
[Sunfyre chittering]

523
00:35:31.588 --> 00:35:33.256
I tried to kill you
to take your place.

524
00:35:35.592 --> 00:35:37.927
You'd be right
to sentence me to die.

525
00:35:44.017 --> 00:35:45.101
Fuck you.

526
00:35:46.978 --> 00:35:47.979
Get up.

527
00:35:55.779 --> 00:35:57.196
We're going to Tumbleton.

528
00:35:57.197 --> 00:35:59.949
My prince cannot.
His dragon abandoned him.

529
00:36:01.117 --> 00:36:03.662
- Who's she?
- My betrothed.

530
00:36:12.712 --> 00:36:16.216
Do you know what's happening
out there?

531
00:36:19.636 --> 00:36:20.637
[softly] No?

532
00:36:22.305 --> 00:36:23.807
Rhaenyra declared me dead.

533
00:36:24.808 --> 00:36:26.433
And after you disappeared.

534
00:36:26.434 --> 00:36:29.562
that little twat Daeron
decided he should be king.

535
00:36:32.857 --> 00:36:34.484
So. here's what
we're going to do.

536
00:36:36.486 --> 00:36:38.987
We're going to find Vhagar.

537
00:36:38.988 --> 00:36:41.990
fly to Tumbleton.
and put Daeron

538
00:36:41.991 --> 00:36:43.992
and that shitheel
Ormund in line.

539
00:36:43.993 --> 00:36:47.413
And then. we're all going
to march on King's Landing

540
00:36:47.414 --> 00:36:49.040
under my banner.

541
00:36:51.084 --> 00:36:54.921
And maybe. when Rhaenyra's
head is on a spike...

542
00:36:56.005 --> 00:36:57.548
and I'm back
on the Iron Throne...

543
00:36:57.549 --> 00:36:59.926
- Aemond.
- [Aegon shushing]

544
00:37:01.386 --> 00:37:03.346
Maybe then...

545
00:37:05.098 --> 00:37:06.433
I'll forgive you...

546
00:37:08.351 --> 00:37:10.937
for trying to fucking kill me.

547
00:37:15.567 --> 00:37:18.193
[Oscar]
<i>Aside from the main gate.
there's one other way in.</i>

548
00:37:18.194 --> 00:37:20.988
A disused postern
on the northeast side.

549
00:37:20.989 --> 00:37:22.114
They've raised
wooden battlements

550
00:37:22.115 --> 00:37:24.074
but the defenses
are incomplete.

551
00:37:24.075 --> 00:37:26.034
so there are vulnerable areas.

552
00:37:26.035 --> 00:37:28.370
particularly the walls
to the southeast.

553
00:37:28.371 --> 00:37:29.706
Simple enough.

554
00:37:30.874 --> 00:37:32.876
I will burn the battlements
over the main gate.

555
00:37:33.877 --> 00:37:35.419
Once they're
clear of resistance.

556
00:37:35.420 --> 00:37:37.713
our van will lead the attack
with Caraxes for cover.

557
00:37:37.714 --> 00:37:40.215
Ulf and Silverwing
will guard the rear.

558
00:37:40.216 --> 00:37:41.884
Rhaenyra's banners will fly

559
00:37:41.885 --> 00:37:43.720
above the holdfast
by nightfall.

560
00:37:46.014 --> 00:37:49.100
Take every care to preserve
the town and its people.
The realm is watching.

561
00:37:50.602 --> 00:37:53.061
The queen's moral standing
must remain absolute.

562
00:37:53.062 --> 00:37:54.229
Sounds boring.

563
00:37:54.230 --> 00:37:55.606
My prince.

564
00:37:55.607 --> 00:37:58.066
My lords.
Movement at the walls.

565
00:37:58.067 --> 00:38:01.571
The enemy has fortified
their numbers with children.

566
00:38:03.490 --> 00:38:05.407
[softly] Gods.

567
00:38:05.408 --> 00:38:07.075
- How many?
- Scores.

568
00:38:07.076 --> 00:38:08.494
All along the battlements.

569
00:38:08.495 --> 00:38:10.330
And that's just
what I could see.

570
00:38:12.415 --> 00:38:14.458
[Oscar]
He's testing you. my prince.

571
00:38:14.459 --> 00:38:16.251
daring you
to use your dragon.

572
00:38:16.252 --> 00:38:17.796
The spineless cunt.

573
00:38:19.297 --> 00:38:22.091
Lord Roderick. are you still
prepared to die for our queen?

574
00:38:22.592 --> 00:38:23.926
Can't fucking wait.

575
00:38:23.927 --> 00:38:25.427
Take your greybeards
over the walls.

576
00:38:25.428 --> 00:38:27.763
overwhelm them with
your northern fighting spirit

577
00:38:27.764 --> 00:38:29.515
and open the gate
from within.

578
00:38:29.516 --> 00:38:32.684
But you are not to die
until you open the gate.

579
00:38:32.685 --> 00:38:34.521
Aye. gate open. then die.

580
00:38:36.147 --> 00:38:37.940
Lord Oscar will lead the flank
as planned.

581
00:38:37.941 --> 00:38:39.942
Ser Garibald has the reserve.

582
00:38:39.943 --> 00:38:41.861
The center is mine.

583
00:38:42.821 --> 00:38:45.657
[♪ dramatic music playing]

584
00:39:01.381 --> 00:39:03.799
This is the House of the Seven.

585
00:39:03.800 --> 00:39:06.344
No arms are to cross
its threshold.

586
00:39:07.345 --> 00:39:10.138
The people
of King's Landing gather.

587
00:39:10.139 --> 00:39:12.642
seeking to know
who is ordained to lead them.

588
00:39:14.185 --> 00:39:16.228
You will give them their answer

589
00:39:16.229 --> 00:39:18.230
by anointing me
for all to see.

590
00:39:18.231 --> 00:39:22.526
I have already told you
that such is impossible.

591
00:39:22.527 --> 00:39:25.696
And now. after Aegon
and his dragon
have been resurrected.

592
00:39:25.697 --> 00:39:28.156
there could be no clearer sign

593
00:39:28.157 --> 00:39:31.995
of whom the gods
have chosen to rule. princess.

594
00:39:32.745 --> 00:39:34.080
I am queen.

595
00:39:36.541 --> 00:39:37.917
The old man forgets.

596
00:39:39.377 --> 00:39:42.380
I wear my father's crown
and sit his throne...

597
00:39:43.339 --> 00:39:45.592
with six dragons at my heel.

598
00:39:46.968 --> 00:39:49.178
You will not deny me
my right a second time.

599
00:39:50.388 --> 00:39:52.890
You may have six dragons.

600
00:39:52.891 --> 00:39:56.560
but I have a Seven-faced god.

601
00:39:56.561 --> 00:40:00.189
I could not possibly
oppose their will.

602
00:40:06.362 --> 00:40:08.281
Then. you name yourself
a traitor.

603
00:40:11.784 --> 00:40:13.453
I am the High Septon
of the Faith.

604
00:40:14.621 --> 00:40:19.082
To harm me is to declare war
upon the Starry Sept.

605
00:40:19.083 --> 00:40:22.712
To damn your soul to the deepest
of the Seven Hells.

606
00:40:26.299 --> 00:40:29.886
You are the blood
of Old Valyria.

607
00:40:31.429 --> 00:40:33.264
You answer
to higher gods than his.

608
00:40:37.769 --> 00:40:40.438
To them. this house...

609
00:40:41.731 --> 00:40:44.275
is an empty work
of brick and stone.

610
00:40:48.655 --> 00:40:51.281
We stand on sacred ground.

611
00:40:51.282 --> 00:40:53.326
- A place of refuge!
- [people gasping]

612
00:40:54.786 --> 00:40:58.247
[grunting. gasping]

613
00:41:19.602 --> 00:41:20.853
[doors close]

614
00:41:24.941 --> 00:41:26.943
[flag flapping softly]

615
00:41:38.454 --> 00:41:39.872
Before his death...

616
00:41:40.999 --> 00:41:44.502
my father.
Viserys the Peaceful...

617
00:41:45.628 --> 00:41:46.879
named me his heir.

618
00:41:49.048 --> 00:41:53.219
Not in secret.
but in ceremony.

619
00:41:54.137 --> 00:41:58.015
Hundreds of lords traveled
hundreds of leagues

620
00:41:58.016 --> 00:42:02.145
to swear fealty to me
before gods and men.

621
00:42:06.649 --> 00:42:10.028
But my rule
was already ordained.

622
00:42:11.154 --> 00:42:13.406
It was prophesied...

623
00:42:14.365 --> 00:42:16.743
long before even Viserys
was born.

624
00:42:21.330 --> 00:42:23.499
<i>It began with the Doom...</i>

625
00:42:24.709 --> 00:42:27.169
<i>when fire and hell erupted</i>

626
00:42:27.170 --> 00:42:30.672
to destroy Old Valyria
and her people.

627
00:42:30.673 --> 00:42:32.592
I need Ulf the Dragonrider!

628
00:42:34.052 --> 00:42:36.053
In there. Find him!

629
00:42:36.054 --> 00:42:38.346
[Rhaenyra]
<i>Only the Targaryens survived.</i>

630
00:42:38.347 --> 00:42:39.681
Where is he?

631
00:42:39.682 --> 00:42:43.268
My family alone were spared.

632
00:42:43.269 --> 00:42:45.271
[people shouting]

633
00:42:49.734 --> 00:42:53.278
The gods summoned my ancestor.

634
00:42:53.279 --> 00:42:56.032
<i>Aegon the Conqueror...</i>

635
00:42:57.033 --> 00:43:01.203
<i>to the Seven Kingdoms
to unite a fractured realm</i>

636
00:43:01.204 --> 00:43:05.541
<i>beneath one banner
of black and red.</i>

637
00:43:07.376 --> 00:43:09.711
They named him

638
00:43:09.712 --> 00:43:12.799
Protector of the World of Men.

639
00:43:14.050 --> 00:43:16.677
His duty. to shield it...

640
00:43:17.386 --> 00:43:21.223
from an ancient
and sinister darkness

641
00:43:21.224 --> 00:43:23.684
that looms in the far North...

642
00:43:24.435 --> 00:43:28.730
beyond the Wall.
beyond the lands of winter.

643
00:43:28.731 --> 00:43:32.484
And only the might of dragons

644
00:43:32.485 --> 00:43:34.987
can stand against it.

645
00:43:36.823 --> 00:43:41.576
The Conqueror passed
this sacred charge

646
00:43:41.577 --> 00:43:46.248
to his chosen descendants.
to the Old King. Jaehaerys.

647
00:43:46.249 --> 00:43:49.459
then to my father.
then to me.

648
00:43:49.460 --> 00:43:53.297
The Hightower line
cannot fulfill this prophecy.

649
00:43:55.508 --> 00:43:58.427
If your world is to survive...

650
00:44:00.096 --> 00:44:03.598
I must light the way.

651
00:44:03.599 --> 00:44:08.019
Because I am
the Shield of the People.

652
00:44:08.020 --> 00:44:12.191
I am Rhaenyra the Chosen.

653
00:44:25.163 --> 00:44:27.706
♪

654
00:44:27.707 --> 00:44:31.626
Lords. knights.
savages. and cutthroats!

655
00:44:31.627 --> 00:44:33.629
[army laughing]

656
00:44:35.214 --> 00:44:37.717
Whether you live or die today...

657
00:44:38.634 --> 00:44:41.386
you will be remembered
in the histories

658
00:44:41.387 --> 00:44:45.016
as those who began
the Hightowers' end!

659
00:44:47.476 --> 00:44:49.812
Grant no mercy!

660
00:44:51.689 --> 00:44:53.232
Give no quarter.

661
00:44:55.484 --> 00:44:58.737
I don't want the best of you.
I want the worst!

662
00:44:58.738 --> 00:45:00.740
- [army shouting]
- [swords and shields clanging]

663
00:45:05.161 --> 00:45:06.912
[drums banging]

664
00:45:06.913 --> 00:45:08.330
[horse whinnying]

665
00:45:08.331 --> 00:45:10.373
[shouting continues]

666
00:45:10.374 --> 00:45:11.500
Go now...

667
00:45:12.668 --> 00:45:14.586
and kill them.

668
00:45:14.587 --> 00:45:17.088
[swords and shields
continue clanging]

669
00:45:17.089 --> 00:45:19.883
[horn blowing]

670
00:45:19.884 --> 00:45:21.384
[shouting]

671
00:45:21.385 --> 00:45:23.845
[shouting continues]

672
00:45:23.846 --> 00:45:25.848
[drums continue banging]

673
00:45:33.022 --> 00:45:34.857
Right. lads!

674
00:45:36.067 --> 00:45:38.443
- Blades out!
- [swords unsheathing]

675
00:45:38.444 --> 00:45:39.946
Bellies in!

676
00:45:43.699 --> 00:45:45.034
[all shout]

677
00:45:47.453 --> 00:45:49.246
[all shout]

678
00:45:49.247 --> 00:45:51.081
[drums continue banging]

679
00:45:51.082 --> 00:45:53.751
[rhythmic shouting
and banging]

680
00:46:06.847 --> 00:46:08.891
- [distant drums banging]
- [Caraxes whistling]

681
00:46:12.061 --> 00:46:14.063
[children whimpering]

682
00:46:18.067 --> 00:46:20.069
[urine trickling]

683
00:46:21.487 --> 00:46:23.489
[children sobbing]

684
00:46:27.493 --> 00:46:28.953
[retching]

685
00:46:32.415 --> 00:46:35.418
[distant rhythmic banging
intensifying]

686
00:46:39.255 --> 00:46:41.756
Siege engines. make ready!

687
00:46:41.757 --> 00:46:43.591
Archers. draw.

688
00:46:43.592 --> 00:46:45.260
- [bows creaking]
- Draw. draw. draw!

689
00:46:45.261 --> 00:46:46.678
[guard] Good aim. lads!

690
00:46:46.679 --> 00:46:49.098
[distant rhythmic banging
continues]

691
00:46:50.766 --> 00:46:52.768
[townspeople whimpering
and sobbing]

692
00:46:54.645 --> 00:46:57.815
[army shouting]

693
00:46:59.108 --> 00:47:01.276
[shouting]

694
00:47:01.277 --> 00:47:03.112
[shouting and banging stop]

695
00:47:09.869 --> 00:47:11.661
Come on. then!

696
00:47:11.662 --> 00:47:14.789
Send your fucking arrows.

697
00:47:14.790 --> 00:47:16.958
you boy-touching cunts!

698
00:47:16.959 --> 00:47:18.627
[arrows thwacking]

699
00:47:22.882 --> 00:47:25.300
- [growling]
- [army shouting]

700
00:47:25.301 --> 00:47:28.304
[all growling and shouting]

701
00:47:34.643 --> 00:47:35.978
Loose!

702
00:47:40.524 --> 00:47:42.526
[army shouting]

703
00:47:47.573 --> 00:47:49.367
[horse whinnying]

704
00:47:56.332 --> 00:47:59.335
[♪ dramatic music playing]

705
00:48:07.385 --> 00:48:08.511
[Roxton] My lord.

706
00:48:09.387 --> 00:48:12.055
There is no sign or word
of Ulf anywhere.

707
00:48:12.056 --> 00:48:14.182
- He's deserted.
- My lord.

708
00:48:14.183 --> 00:48:15.559
The battle has begun.

709
00:48:17.019 --> 00:48:19.354
- You don't say?
- Yes. my lord.

710
00:48:19.355 --> 00:48:20.855
It appears Daemon Targaryen

711
00:48:20.856 --> 00:48:22.691
did not accept
King Daeron's terms.

712
00:48:26.362 --> 00:48:27.363
Terms?

713
00:48:29.198 --> 00:48:30.573
Speak!

714
00:48:30.574 --> 00:48:32.742
King Daeron.
he sent Ser Gwayne

715
00:48:32.743 --> 00:48:35.078
to treat with the enemy
under a banner of peace.

716
00:48:35.079 --> 00:48:38.373
He freed the Sea Snake.
my lord. as part of the bargain.

717
00:48:38.374 --> 00:48:41.627
[Roxton]
Continue the search.
Find Ulf the Dragonrider.

718
00:48:49.051 --> 00:48:52.096
[soldiers shouting]

719
00:48:54.890 --> 00:48:56.266
Where is the prince?

720
00:48:56.267 --> 00:48:57.560
The king?

721
00:48:59.103 --> 00:49:01.105
- [army shouting]
- [arrows whizzing]

722
00:49:06.902 --> 00:49:08.571
Ladders! The ladders!

723
00:49:09.738 --> 00:49:10.738
[thud]

724
00:49:10.739 --> 00:49:11.949
Oil!

725
00:49:14.076 --> 00:49:15.744
[screaming]

726
00:49:17.329 --> 00:49:19.331
- [screaming]
- [sizzling]

727
00:49:20.583 --> 00:49:23.586
[♪ dramatic music playing]

728
00:49:29.925 --> 00:49:31.594
Advance!

729
00:49:43.105 --> 00:49:44.607
South wall!

730
00:49:50.488 --> 00:49:51.864
[shouting]

731
00:49:58.287 --> 00:49:59.622
[screaming]

732
00:50:04.502 --> 00:50:06.504
[shouting]

733
00:50:10.841 --> 00:50:11.842
[shouting]

734
00:50:19.642 --> 00:50:20.851
[soft thud]

735
00:50:24.355 --> 00:50:26.189
[Hightower captain] Arrows!

736
00:50:26.190 --> 00:50:28.150
Light the trenches!

737
00:50:37.743 --> 00:50:39.828
[soldiers screaming]

738
00:50:51.006 --> 00:50:54.385
Your Grace. I cannot find
Ser Ulf the White.

739
00:50:57.012 --> 00:50:59.514
What do you mean.
you cannot find him?

740
00:50:59.515 --> 00:51:02.517
He has a very large dragon.

741
00:51:02.518 --> 00:51:05.604
Begging pardon. Your Grace.
He is not with his dragon.

742
00:51:11.360 --> 00:51:12.444
[arrow thwacking]

743
00:51:16.240 --> 00:51:17.616
Turret!

744
00:51:21.287 --> 00:51:23.289
[soldiers shouting]

745
00:51:26.458 --> 00:51:27.709
[Roxton] Stop!

746
00:51:27.710 --> 00:51:29.712
Find that fucking gate. lads!

747
00:51:30.963 --> 00:51:32.047
Take them.

748
00:51:33.132 --> 00:51:35.216
- [knight] Draw swords!
- [laughing]

749
00:51:35.217 --> 00:51:36.926
- [Roderick] Kill them!
- Forward!

750
00:51:36.927 --> 00:51:39.555
- [shouting]
- [swords clanging]

751
00:51:40.639 --> 00:51:42.933
[dragon bellowing]

752
00:51:48.480 --> 00:51:50.732
Is that Hugh Hammer's dragon?

753
00:51:50.733 --> 00:51:52.735
Hugh is meant to be guarding
King's Landing.

754
00:51:54.153 --> 00:51:55.613
Learn why he's here.

755
00:52:01.744 --> 00:52:04.747
[♪ dramatic music playing]

756
00:52:08.917 --> 00:52:11.753
Center! Form on me!

757
00:52:11.754 --> 00:52:12.921
Caraxes!

758
00:52:14.006 --> 00:52:16.008
[heavy footfall]

759
00:52:20.137 --> 00:52:22.139
[horses whinnying]

760
00:52:27.269 --> 00:52:29.772
- At ready!
- Hold your positions!

761
00:52:34.109 --> 00:52:36.152
Dragon!

762
00:52:36.153 --> 00:52:38.113
Bring down the rider!

763
00:52:39.448 --> 00:52:41.616
[arrows whizzing]

764
00:52:41.617 --> 00:52:42.618
<i>Dracarys!</i>

765
00:52:44.536 --> 00:52:46.955
[soldiers screaming]

766
00:52:55.798 --> 00:52:58.132
Move! Get down there!

767
00:52:58.133 --> 00:52:59.717
- Through the doors!
- [children crying]

768
00:52:59.718 --> 00:53:00.719
Come on!

769
00:53:02.054 --> 00:53:04.305
Get out of the way!

770
00:53:04.306 --> 00:53:05.474
Move!

771
00:53:06.308 --> 00:53:09.812
- [Caraxes screeching]
- [children screaming]

772
00:53:14.358 --> 00:53:15.693
<i>Dracarys!</i>

773
00:53:31.542 --> 00:53:34.044
[screeching]

774
00:53:36.839 --> 00:53:39.842
[♪ dramatic music playing]

775
00:53:44.596 --> 00:53:46.849
Forward!

776
00:53:47.391 --> 00:53:48.684
[horses whinnying]

777
00:53:54.189 --> 00:53:56.024
[arrows whizzing]

778
00:53:57.025 --> 00:53:58.193
[horse whinnying]

779
00:54:03.615 --> 00:54:04.867
[shouting]

780
00:54:06.243 --> 00:54:07.536
[whinnying]

781
00:54:10.247 --> 00:54:13.083
[soldiers shouting]

782
00:54:17.963 --> 00:54:19.798
[horn blowing]

783
00:54:21.550 --> 00:54:22.718
[soldier]
To the main gates!

784
00:54:25.262 --> 00:54:27.264
That's the gates
open then. lads.

785
00:54:29.099 --> 00:54:31.893
- And we're still fucking alive.
- [soldiers shouting]

786
00:54:31.894 --> 00:54:34.061
Find me that boy king.

787
00:54:34.062 --> 00:54:35.105
Go now!

788
00:54:37.274 --> 00:54:39.067
I want Lord Hightower.

789
00:54:41.069 --> 00:54:43.071
[light snoring]

790
00:54:50.078 --> 00:54:52.080
[quick footsteps approaching]

791
00:54:53.916 --> 00:54:54.917
[banging]

792
00:54:57.044 --> 00:54:59.254
- [soldier gagging]
- Get him out!

793
00:55:00.088 --> 00:55:01.256
[groaning]

794
00:55:02.257 --> 00:55:05.260
- Get up!
- You worthless sot!

795
00:55:05.928 --> 00:55:08.972
All you had to do was sit
on your fucking dragon!

796
00:55:10.265 --> 00:55:12.433
They're inside the walls!

797
00:55:12.434 --> 00:55:14.937
You useless baseborn stump!

798
00:55:16.188 --> 00:55:17.648
You may have cost us everything.

799
00:55:18.607 --> 00:55:21.692
Now. get back on that beast.

800
00:55:21.693 --> 00:55:23.195
and do as you've been told!

801
00:55:27.115 --> 00:55:29.117
[townspeople screaming]

802
00:55:31.453 --> 00:55:32.454
[gasps]

803
00:55:33.997 --> 00:55:36.208
Ormund Hightower!

804
00:55:42.214 --> 00:55:43.548
[sword stabbing]

805
00:55:43.549 --> 00:55:45.509
[Hugh]
Kat. where are you?

806
00:55:49.179 --> 00:55:50.305
Kat!

807
00:55:54.226 --> 00:55:56.519
Ormund Hightower!

808
00:55:56.520 --> 00:55:57.855
[Roxton] Kinslayer!

809
00:56:04.653 --> 00:56:06.238
Babe killer.

810
00:56:07.865 --> 00:56:09.491
Heathen!

811
00:56:18.709 --> 00:56:20.043
[bellowing]

812
00:56:22.212 --> 00:56:24.964
Ser Ulf. I have orders
from Prince Daemon

813
00:56:24.965 --> 00:56:27.174
to make certain that you
and your dragon are at the--

814
00:56:27.175 --> 00:56:28.218
[exclaiming]

815
00:56:37.060 --> 00:56:39.021
- [dragon snarling]
- Daeron!

816
00:56:39.897 --> 00:56:41.898
Your parlay failed.

817
00:56:41.899 --> 00:56:44.525
Daemon's overwhelmed the city.

818
00:56:44.526 --> 00:56:45.694
You will die.

819
00:56:46.695 --> 00:56:49.031
But I won't be remembered
a craven.

820
00:56:49.781 --> 00:56:52.366
I have fought
beside other brave men

821
00:56:52.367 --> 00:56:55.953
who believed that death
was the only path to glory.

822
00:56:55.954 --> 00:56:58.039
Do not die for Ormund's vanity.

823
00:56:58.040 --> 00:57:00.583
[Tessarion snarling]

824
00:57:00.584 --> 00:57:02.251
My boy.

825
00:57:02.252 --> 00:57:03.712
My boy. please.

826
00:57:06.256 --> 00:57:07.381
Please!

827
00:57:07.382 --> 00:57:08.467
- [Tessarion bellowing]
- Stay back.

828
00:57:10.552 --> 00:57:12.554
[panting]

829
00:57:14.389 --> 00:57:16.391
[Tessarion snarling]

830
00:57:18.644 --> 00:57:19.728
[whispering]
Stay back.

831
00:57:20.979 --> 00:57:22.606
You'll have to come
through me then.

832
00:57:24.232 --> 00:57:26.234
[Tessarion screeching]

833
00:57:35.160 --> 00:57:37.579
[army cheering]

834
00:57:41.458 --> 00:57:44.461
[♪ dramatic music playing]

835
00:57:55.430 --> 00:57:57.432
[Ulf]
<i>Dracarys!</i>

836
00:58:10.278 --> 00:58:12.280
[people screaming]

837
00:58:17.995 --> 00:58:19.495
[dragon screeching]

838
00:58:19.496 --> 00:58:20.998
[Roxton] There you are.

839
00:58:22.290 --> 00:58:23.458
[shouting]

840
00:58:36.972 --> 00:58:38.974
[Silverwing bellowing]

841
00:58:40.976 --> 00:58:42.686
There's Ormund's piece
on the board.

842
00:58:43.729 --> 00:58:45.355
Perhaps we'll survive the day.

843
00:58:50.485 --> 00:58:52.904
- [Silverwing bellowing]
- Clear a path!

844
00:59:13.008 --> 00:59:15.010
[screaming]

845
00:59:27.355 --> 00:59:28.732
[growling]

846
00:59:30.734 --> 00:59:32.736
[grunting. shouting]

847
00:59:42.037 --> 00:59:43.371
[shouting]

848
00:59:46.458 --> 00:59:48.460
[Silverwing bellowing]

849
00:59:55.133 --> 00:59:56.468
[shouting]

850
01:00:06.895 --> 01:00:08.230
- [blade stabbing]
- [grunting]

851
01:00:11.399 --> 01:00:13.401
[screaming]

852
01:00:15.237 --> 01:00:16.905
- [retching]
- [Roderick shouting]

853
01:00:20.075 --> 01:00:22.077
[screaming]

854
01:00:23.411 --> 01:00:25.830
That's a proper fucking.

855
01:00:25.831 --> 01:00:27.624
By the North.

856
01:00:31.253 --> 01:00:33.255
[Silverwing roaring]

857
01:00:39.845 --> 01:00:41.804
Fuck you. too.

858
01:00:41.805 --> 01:00:44.598
- [laughing]
- No. No!

859
01:00:44.599 --> 01:00:45.767
[screaming]

860
01:00:59.531 --> 01:01:01.449
Move! Find cover!

861
01:01:07.539 --> 01:01:09.332
[screaming]

862
01:01:19.009 --> 01:01:20.302
[Silverwing bellowing]

863
01:01:38.028 --> 01:01:40.030
[muffled rumbling]

864
01:01:47.078 --> 01:01:49.080
[muffled rumbling continues]

865
01:01:53.668 --> 01:01:55.212
[muffled screeching]

866
01:02:03.887 --> 01:02:06.181
[muffled rumbling continues]

867
01:02:13.521 --> 01:02:15.774
[muffled] Where are you?!

868
01:02:16.942 --> 01:02:18.860
[muffled clanging]

869
01:02:26.534 --> 01:02:29.746
[♪ soft. somber music playing]

870
01:02:38.088 --> 01:02:40.090
[muffled hoofbeats]

871
01:02:47.472 --> 01:02:49.474
[woman sobbing]

872
01:02:51.309 --> 01:02:53.311
[muffled rumbling continues]

873
01:03:00.652 --> 01:03:03.655
[♪ soft. somber music
continues playing]

874
01:03:12.289 --> 01:03:14.291
[muffled rumbling continues]

875
01:03:23.925 --> 01:03:26.928
[♪ soft. somber music
continues playing]

876
01:03:46.156 --> 01:03:47.365
[shouting]

877
01:03:48.366 --> 01:03:49.992
Ulf has turned.

878
01:03:49.993 --> 01:03:51.494
The town is lost.

879
01:03:52.787 --> 01:03:54.372
We are leaving.

880
01:03:59.210 --> 01:04:01.962
[dragon screeching]

881
01:04:01.963 --> 01:04:04.966
♪

882
01:04:16.728 --> 01:04:19.731
[♪ soft. somber music
continues playing]

883
01:04:56.601 --> 01:04:59.604
♪

884
01:05:06.694 --> 01:05:08.405
[weakly] Daeron.

885
01:05:11.449 --> 01:05:13.118
[coughing]

886
01:05:14.369 --> 01:05:16.371
[gasping] Daeron.

887
01:05:32.303 --> 01:05:35.723
[♪ soft. somber music
continues playing]

888
01:05:40.311 --> 01:05:42.730
Kat. Kat!

889
01:05:49.320 --> 01:05:51.071
[screaming]

890
01:05:51.072 --> 01:05:54.075
[♪ somber music
continues playing]

891
01:06:32.113 --> 01:06:33.364
[Elinda] My queen!

892
01:06:47.128 --> 01:06:50.131
[♪ somber music
continues playing]

893
01:07:18.159 --> 01:07:21.162
♪

894
01:07:29.921 --> 01:07:31.923
[butterfly wings flapping]

895
01:07:56.281 --> 01:07:58.283
[♪ music ends]

896
01:08:01.452 --> 01:08:03.288
[wind whistling]

897
01:08:09.043 --> 01:08:12.463
[♪ soft. dramatic music playing]

898
01:08:32.942 --> 01:08:35.945
[♪ music intensifying]

899
01:08:49.125 --> 01:08:50.418
[♪ music fades]

900
01:08:51.305 --> 01:09:51.727
